BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (The opener is where the mechanics get specific. Dennis Brown says the hardest part of a cold call is the first) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (5 to 15 seconds, and retires stale lines like "trucks in your area," "save you money," and "network of over) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (10,000 trucks" as delivering very low return on investment. Brown's replacement, adapted from a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (sales-training call Brown personally received, runs: "hey John, John this is Dennis, you're most likely going) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (to hate me, I'm a freight broker, so do you want to hang up now or will you give me 30 seconds to tell you) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (why I'm calling" [-_16MS3HWhA @ 00:04:17]. A yes buys 30, 60 or 90 seconds for a hook built on market) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (intelligence and a request for a quick follow-up call. Krause kills yes/no openers like "is now a good time?") Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (because 9.5 out of 10 times the answer was "in the middle of something," and instead asks, with no name) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (intro, whether the prospect might help with "something transportation related by chance" [LNT0OaH1J8s @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (00:03:25]. Krause backs this with Gong data: "did I catch you at a bad time" books under 1%, 40% worse) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (than average, while naming the reason upfront roughly doubles the odds [r0gf3CDabxw @ 00:09:19]. One) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (researched nugget mentioned inside the first ten seconds, Krause adds, beats "99.9%" of callers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm ([LNT0OaH1J8s @ 00:14:32].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (Objection handling is scripted down to the pause. On the pet food account, the answer to "we don't use) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (brokers" was "Good. I'm glad to hear it," then silence, then: "several of my customers said the exact same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (thing... Do you want to know why they eventually decided to work with us?" [knW5LzcUJIw @ 00:01:28].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (The ask was one test load with no lane replacement and no commitment; it arrived within about two weeks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (at roughly $1,500 revenue and $150 gross profit, and a post-delivery "When's the next load on that lane) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (shipping?" won the next one on the spot [knW5LzcUJIw @ 00:04:03]. Krause's NEPQ playbook handles) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm ("we're happy" with "I'm not quite sure if we'd even be the right fit for you yet," a 2 to 3 second pause, and a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (frequency question about how often carriers fall off a load last minute [ZG3bMHTCx1Y @ 00:03:18]. For) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm ("send me your rates," Krause warns that giving a number puts you "in a bidding war," so reframe around) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (lead times, appointments and late penalties, then ask for the biggest operational challenge. In the longer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (script, Krause sorts objections into reflex \(agree, then ask\), wound \(label it\) and deflection \(take it literally) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (and add one question\), noting "none of those is a no" [r0gf3CDabxw @ 00:17:41].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm (The follow-up and the math close the loop. Krause defines the first call's only goal as becoming the broker) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (the shipper would take a second call from, with the number saved as backup, then sends a one-paragraph) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (email within the hour and holds the setup packet \(agreement, W9, insurance\) until there is a load) Tj ET
