BT /F2 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 755.00 Tm (THE BIG MONEY PLAYBOOKS) Tj ET
0.6 w 54.00 747.00 m 558.00 747.00 l S
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Title: Close Out With BOL and Invoice) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (Action: Get in and out times initialed on the BOL, keep the gate tickets and photos, invoice, and follow up) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (until the charge lands on settlement.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (Detail: Have someone at the facility write and initial the in and out times on the bill of lading, and photograph) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (everything. Then submit the claim with the documentation attached [Think Trucking - uHIZpxSLN-c @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (00:07:16]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (The street rate card is wide, and practitioners quote it to the dollar. The spread between low and high offers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (is where negotiation lives. Trucking Territory works with $30 for each extra hour past two, and $100 to $150) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (per night of layover when the broker is reasonable [Q-HgB9nn1jI @ 00:03:17]. Pauline Nabacwa reports the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (floor going lower: brokers offering $12, $15 or $20 an hour, or a flat $100, $150 or $200 for the whole wait.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (Pauline calls that cheap change against what the truck gives up [fpu1Fhdo9Vs @ 00:03:41]. Ernest at Never) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (Stop Trucking adds the cap buried in many policies: a typical broker policy pays $50 an hour up to a $250) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (maximum, then flips to layover. Layover commonly lands at $200 to $250 a day, roughly $10 to $12 an hour) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (once divided by 24. TONU is a flat $150 whether the driver deadheaded two miles or 200 [tvnlRLMXRJ4 @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (00:05:33]. Nate Cross at Freight 360 prices layover higher on the broker side, at around $500 depending on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (equipment. Nate sets TONU near $200 and extra stops at $50 to $100 each. Lumpers run roughly $75 up to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm ($200, reimbursed against a receipt or advanced to the driver up front [A7rlv69JAj8 @ 00:05:06].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (Collection runs on a timed email sequence, and Craig Bliss hands it out nearly word for word. On arrival, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (carrier emails the broker something like: driver has arrived at the shipper as of 1300, detention will start at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (1500 at $50 per hour, and a heads-up will follow before it starts [WU9uuEFffXU @ 00:02:33]. At about 90) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (minutes, a second email in the same chain notes the driver is still not loaded at 1430 and offers to help) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (speed loading. At expiry, a third email says detention is now running. After loading, a final email carries total) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (charges plus the bill of lading with in and out times. Think Trucking runs the same five-step drill. First, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (clause goes on the rate con. Second, the carrier sends a timestamped written arrival notice rather than a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (phone call. Third comes a warning before free time ends. Fourth, in and out times go on the BOL, initialed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (by facility staff, with gate tickets and photos kept. Fifth, the invoice is chased until it lands on settlement) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm ([uHIZpxSLN-c @ 00:07:00]. Trucking Territory adds a field tactic: the two-hour call itself can push the broker) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (to get the truck loaded faster to save money. If the next pickup is at risk, call that broker too and try to move) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (the appointment to the next day [Q-HgB9nn1jI @ 00:04:47].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (On the broker side, the mechanics turn on approval paperwork and, for some, margin. Brandon Scott emails) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm (the shipper the situation and the PO number, then gets the PO approved for detention. Brandon then issues) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm (the carrier a new rate confirmation showing the accumulated detention hours, so the final invoice includes it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm ([V11p0IBJsTk @ 00:08:16]. Freight 360 does the same on TONU. The broker confirms what the customer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (typically pays on cancellation and invoices the customer the $200. The broker then cuts a fresh rate con to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.35 Tm (the driver for $200 and makes zero margin on the transaction [7sfi19fbIzU @ 00:02:52]. Brandon Manney) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.12 Tm (teaches the opposite money play: ask every shipper its detention and layover rates during the sale, then pay) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 160.90 Tm (the carrier less than collected. In Manney's example, a shipper pays $200 an hour for two hours, $400 total.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 145.67 Tm (The broker pays the carrier $100 an hour and keeps $200, or collects $500 on a layover and pays $400 or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 130.45 Tm ($300 [8Mhf3iqBflw @ 00:04:09]. Carriers can flip the paperwork too. Tim at Freight Master Resources has) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 115.22 Tm (carriers draft their own detention and layover terms as a PDF and send them for signature through) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 100.00 Tm (DocuSign or similar. That lets them negotiate from $75 an hour down to $40 or $50 instead of accepting $20) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 84.77 Tm (to $25 after three or four hours [1Fdc8KYk8M0 @ 00:07:39].) Tj ET
