0.6 w 54.00 747.00 m 558.00 747.00 l S
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Detail: Consignees should not be rushed by drivers, should open crates to check for concealed damage,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (should never refuse the shipment, and should report concealed damage within five days [Quote Factory -) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (Ti9MeFBKijM @ 00:04:20]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (Step: 3) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (Title: File a compliant written claim) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (Action: Send a formal written claim to the motor carrier with a specific dollar amount, a commercial invoice,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (and the carrier named as liable.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (Detail: A notated bill of lading or a phone call does not meet the filing requirements, and retail value cannot) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (be claimed under Carmack. Then hold the carrier to its 30-day acknowledgment and 120-day disposition) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (deadlines [LOGISTICS RISK EXPERT by Cassandra Gaines - Ig6sI3O1a14 @ 00:06:19]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (Step: 4) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (Title: Move inside 48 hours on theft) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (Action: Hand CargoNet, law enforcement, and the insurer the driver identity, timeline, and location data) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (immediately.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (Detail: Palmer's instruction is to be a good victim: report properly and timely within about 24 to 48 hours,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (because calling three months later with no driver, time, or location drops recovery odds to roughly zero) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm ([CargoRex - xQYjaYAvyms @ 00:13:43]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (Claim filing is where brokers get taken advantage of. Gaines lays out the minimum filing requirements from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (the federal regulations she tells operators to look up at 49 CFR Part 370. First, the claim must be a formal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (written communication to the motor carrier. Notating the bill of lading does not count, and neither does) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (phoning in that a couple of pallets are missing. Second, it must state a specific dollar amount, normally) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (backed by a commercial invoice, because retail value is off the table under Carmack. Third, it must name) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (the carrier as the liable party [Ig6sI3O1a14 @ 00:06:19]. Brent of Anderson Trucking Service walks through) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (the broker's side of the workflow. The broker logs the claim and forwards it to the claims department. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (department requests the original BOL, the original paid freight bill, the original or a certified invoice, and any) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (photo, video, or other proof. That package goes to the customer and the carrier, the carrier submits it to its) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (insurer, and the agent facilitates communication from there [id2FXFnynHM @ 00:00:43]. Quote Factory) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (adds the hard edges. The claim covers cost incurred, not profit, measured as original value minus damaged) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (value. Concealed damage and shortages must be reported within five days. Damaged freight should be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (retained rather than refused, and the freight bill gets paid regardless of damage, loss, or theft [Ti9MeFBKijM) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm (@ 00:05:41].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm (On pre-load verification, Freight 360 runs the most detailed playbook. A certificate of insurance is usually) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm (one or two pages, while the actual policy contract is most likely about 60 pages. When a carrier says 'yeah,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (it covers it' on a load of eggs, the broker is just taking their word for it [qTcDOmwZMjI @ 00:23:12]. The fix is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.35 Tm (to pull the certificate from an authorized third party such as Highway, AssureAssist, or RMIS rather than) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.12 Tm (from the carrier or dispatcher. Then have the carrier's insurance agent email the certificate, with the carrier) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 160.90 Tm (on copy, and confirm in writing that the commodity is covered in the event of a claim. This matters most for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 145.67 Tm (the usual exclusions: eggs, frozen seafood, firearms, electronics, and alcohol [qTcDOmwZMjI @ 00:27:38].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 130.45 Tm (Ben of Freight 360 warns that adding reefer breakdown can bring 10 to 20 more exclusions, so the carrier) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 115.22 Tm (can end up with less coverage. The suggested workaround is to feed the policy to an LLM, have it find and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 100.00 Tm (summarize the exclusions, and use that list to ask the agent sharper questions [qTcDOmwZMjI @ 00:25:02].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 84.77 Tm (Large brokerages also ask carriers on a recorded line whether anything on the vehicle needs service,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 69.55 Tm (because maintenance fine print can void cargo coverage. That might be an oil light the driver did not get to) Tj ET
